    contentEn: "<h2>Private Transfer from Hotel Alfonso to Zaragoza Airport</h2>\n<p>Hotel Alfonso sits on the corner of Calle Coso and Calle Alfonso, two of the busiest and most historic streets running through the heart of Zaragoza, which makes checkout here a genuinely central departure rather than one from a quiet side street. Once you've settled your bill and confirmed your flight time, a private chauffeur can have you at Zaragoza Airport (ZAZ) in around 20 minutes, covering roughly 17 kilometres from this corner of the historic centre out to the terminal on the city's western edge. Rather than stepping out onto Calle Coso to flag down a passing taxi among the crowds and shopfronts, your car is scheduled to be waiting at an agreed point outside the hotel at the exact time you specify.</p>\n<p>With 120 rooms spread across a building positioned directly on Calle Coso, one of Zaragoza's main historic thoroughfares, Hotel Alfonso sits closer to the flow of city traffic than hotels tucked deeper into the pedestrian lanes of the old town. That's generally an advantage on departure morning — a private car can usually reach a point close to the hotel entrance without needing to navigate restricted pedestrian streets first, though the corner location does mean coordinating an exact pickup spot in advance, since Calle Coso itself carries a steady flow of both pedestrians and vehicles throughout the day.</p>\n<p>Booking your transfer in advance through <a href=\"/get-a-quote/\">get a quote</a> means your pickup time, vehicle, and price are agreed before you check out, with your flight number tracked automatically so a delay or an earlier departure doesn't turn your morning into a scramble for alternative transport.</p>\n<h2>Planning Your Departure from Calle Coso</h2>\n<h3>How Much Time to Allow Before Your Flight</h3>\n<p>Allow around two hours from hotel departure to boarding for a typical flight from Zaragoza Airport, which means leaving Hotel Alfonso roughly two hours and 20 minutes before your scheduled departure once the drive itself is included. ZAZ's compact, single terminal generally keeps this margin comfortable, though it's worth padding out slightly during the Fiestas del Pilar in October, when Calle Coso and the surrounding streets fill with crowds, processions, and stalls that can slow the first minutes of any departure from this exact corner of the city.</p>\n<p>Early mornings before the shops along Calle Coso open for the day tend to offer the smoothest run to the airport, while Saturday afternoons, when the street is at its busiest with shoppers, can add a few extra minutes to the initial pull away from the hotel.</p>\n<h3>Traffic Leaving the Historic Centre via Calle Coso</h3>\n<p>Because Calle Coso is one of the wider, more vehicle-accessible streets running through Zaragoza's old town, leaving from Hotel Alfonso is generally more straightforward than from hotels set back in the narrower pedestrian lanes nearby — but the street still carries dense pedestrian and vehicle traffic through the middle of the day, and a driver who knows the flow of Calle Coso and the quickest connecting route to the Ebro crossing will typically outperform a route chosen purely by navigation app.</p>\n<p>Once past the historic centre and across the river, the drive toward Zaragoza Airport is usually smooth, with light traffic outside the standard morning and evening commuting windows.</p>\n<h3>The Pickup Point Outside the Hotel</h3>\n<p>Given the hotel's position directly on Calle Coso, your driver will typically arrange pickup at a specific, agreed point close to the entrance rather than attempting to stop in the busiest stretch of the street itself. Hotel staff are experienced in coordinating this with private transfer drivers, and confirming your flight number and preferred time in advance means the exact spot is settled before you come down with your luggage.</p>\n<h2>Inside Hotel Alfonso</h2>\n<p>Hotel Alfonso offers 120 rooms in a building that anchors the corner of Calle Coso and Calle Alfonso, putting it within easy walking distance of the Basílica del Pilar, La Seo, and the rest of Zaragoza's historic centre. The hotel is unusual among the city's central properties in offering both an outdoor rooftop pool, open during the summer months, and an indoor pool available year-round — a genuine amenity advantage for guests visiting outside the warmer season.</p>\n<p>That combination of a genuinely central address on one of Zaragoza's principal historic streets, along with year-round pool access, makes Hotel Alfonso a practical choice for travellers who want to be within walking distance of the main sights without sacrificing hotel amenities during a shoulder-season or winter visit. Guests checking out for an early flight can still fit in a swim beforehand thanks to the indoor pool, an option not every central Zaragoza hotel can offer outside the summer months.</p>\n<h2>Private Transfer versus Taxi from Hotel Alfonso</h2>\n<p>Taxis do pass along Calle Coso regularly, given its status as one of the busier streets in central Zaragoza, but hailing one during peak pedestrian hours or festival periods can still mean a wait, and a wait is the last thing you want with a flight to catch. A pre-booked private transfer removes that uncertainty entirely, with a car scheduled for your exact time and pickup point regardless of how busy the street happens to be that day.</p>\n<p>A fixed price agreed before you travel, along with a driver tracking your flight number, means the return to the airport is one less thing to think about on a morning that likely already includes finishing packing and checking out.</p>\n<h2>Zaragoza Airport: A Straightforward Departure</h2>\n<p>Zaragoza Airport operates a single, compact passenger terminal, so there's no confusion over where to head once you arrive, unlike the larger multi-terminal airports in Madrid or Barcelona. The airport is internationally notable chiefly for cargo rather than passenger numbers — the adjacent PLAZA logistics platform makes ZAZ Spain's second-busiest cargo airport after Madrid-Barajas — but that freight traffic runs entirely separately from the passenger side, keeping check-in and security quick. Your driver drops you at the terminal front, comfortably within the 20-minute window from the hotel.</p>\n<h2>Booking Your Transfer in Advance</h2>\n<p>A transfer arranged ahead of time locks in a fixed price and removes one more thing to plan around on departure morning. Review general details on our <a href=\"/zaragoza-airport-transfer/\">Zaragoza airport transfer</a> page, see our <a href=\"/city-to-city-transfers/\">city-to-city transfers</a> service if your trip continues elsewhere in Spain, or request a <a href=\"/get-a-quote/\">fixed-price quote</a> once your flight is confirmed. Live departure information is available on <a href=\"https://www.aena.es\">aena.es</a> before you head down.</p>",
